{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkCdTfQkBRPn5ZYXyJ8U","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The contract is at `contract/claim.compact` and compiles cleanly. I ran `compact compile` on it and it produced the `compiler`, `contract`, `keys` and `zkir` outputs. I haven't run the contract itself.\n\n- **Witness and circuits:** `secretKey()` is the only witness. `publicKey(sk)` is an exported pure circuit that returns `persistentHash([pad(32,\"claim:pk:\"), sk])`. `claim()` is exported.\n- **Privacy:** the ledger never stores the public key. `claim()` stores a nullifier, `persistentHash([pad(32,\"claim:nullifier:\"), sk])`, in a `nullifiers` set. It uses a different domain separator from `publicKey`, so nobody can compute a user's nullifier from their public key. Looking at the ledger, you can't tell whether a given public key has claimed.\n- **Double-claim:** `claim()` asserts the nullifier isn't already in the set, then inserts it and calls `claims.increment(1)`. A second claim with the same secret key fails with \"Already claimed\".\n- **Disclosure:** the nullifier is wrapped in `disclose(...)` because it is written to the public ledger. It's a one-way hash, so the secret key stays private."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":78,"cache_read_input_tokens":22043,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":78},"output_tokens":421,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f115a5df-d6ad-4d00-a86d-ba174e6714a4","uuid":"6e6414fa-e6f2-4d7c-b402-3ccc7f277933","timestamp":"2026-11-05T17:47:59.332Z","request_id":"req_011CgkCdTJ5fEtJiBHu3y7JS"}
